course: dictionary
lesson: 15199
title: Select: choosing with care
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To select means to choose one thing, or some things, from a group, and to do it carefully. «Mia had to select one book from the shelf for the reading prize.» She looked at them all before she picked the one she liked best.
explain: Select can also be about a computer screen. «Click and drag to select the words you want to copy.» Here you highlight the text so the computer knows what to work on. In sport, a coach can select a player: «Ravi was selected for the football team.»
explain: As an adjective, select is formal and means only for a small group of the best or richest people. «The club is select, so only fifty members can join.» You will meet this less often, so check the words around it to be sure of the meaning.
fact: Select is a verb: select, selects, selected, selecting.
fact: «Select» means to choose someone or something from a group, carefully.
fact: On a computer, to select means to click on or highlight something on a screen.
fact: In maths, «select a card at random» means pick one card by chance, without choosing which one on purpose.
fact: Useful phrases: select from, select at random, be selected for.
exercise: «Please select one fruit from the basket.» What does select mean here? | Throw away all the fruit | *Choose one carefully | Eat the basket | Count the baskets
exercise: Your teacher says, «Select the word you want to change.» What do you do on the computer? | *Highlight the word on the screen | Sing the word aloud | Draw a picture of the word | Close the computer
exercise: «Lena was selected for the school netball team.» What does selected mean? | *Chosen from a group | Sent home early | Given a new kit from the shop | Forgotten by the coach
test: «Select a counter at random from the bag.» What does at random mean? | Only the red ones | The biggest one first | *By chance, without choosing which one on purpose | Using a ruler to measure
test: Which phrase means that someone was picked for a team? | Selected by the shop | *Be selected for | Select at random | Select from
exam: Which sentence uses select as a formal adjective? | «Lena selects her lunch every day.» | «Click here to select the picture.» | *«The club is select: only the best members may join.» | «I will select a pen from the pot.»
